{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/713235-bill-cipher-strix","id":713235,"title":"Bill Cipher = Strix?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-21T17:05:47-07:00","id":713235,"title":"Bill Cipher = Strix?","content":"Anyone here who's watched the show <i>Gravity Falls</i> is obviously familiar with its weirdness and its almost WoD tone, albeit somewhat more lighthearted\u2014sometimes. (It's almost like <i>Innocents</i> with a hint of <i>Blood and Smoke</i> when it's gotten into gear.)<br /> <br /> This show has a lot of owl motifs going on too, at least once per episode. One episode even has a long section of text (you have to freeze frame to read it all) about owls and secret societies.<br /> <br /> In another episode one character grabs another whom he hasn't seen in awhile and refuses to let him go anywhere until he shines a flashlight into their eyes to be sure there isn't any yellow in them.<br /> <br /> That aside, when the character Bill has shown up, and demonstrated his abilities and persona, has anyone else immediately thought: 'Holy shit, he's one of the owls!'<br /> <br /> He even makes deals (and goes back on them or warps them to his liking), and goes to lengths to do harm to a body he possesses\u2014complete with eyes turning bright yellow and slitted\u2014cackling &quot;Hah, pain is <i>hilarious</i>!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 10-21-2015, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T19:21:11-07:00","id":713474,"title":"","content":"I don't know. While he might make a good inspiration, he feels both more and less powerful than I think of when I consider the Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T19:42:39-07:00","id":713510,"title":"","content":"I'll admit he's a bit asymmetrical (and I also just found another thread elsewhere in another sub forum where someone describes him in more demonic or spirit related terms), but still, the possession angle, the yellow eyes, and the owl themes still are an amusing set of traits. At the very least, though, he does make a good inspiration\u2014and he does kind of remind me of one of the Strix from a previous chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:00:14-07:00","id":714030,"title":"","content":"If I understand correctly, he's called a demon, but he's from a realm adjacent only to the world of the mind, yeah? He's got some aesthetics going on (chiefly by way of Twin Peaks), but I'd come at him from a Mage angle. He's a powerful goetic demon that wants to make its mark felt much more directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:09:31-07:00","id":714035,"title":"","content":"I could easily imagine a strix with his <i>personality</i>, but yeah, power-wise he's on a whole other level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:22:35-07:00","id":714042,"title":"","content":"Honestly he seems more God-Machiney to me. Not that he acts like the Machine itself, but that he's somehow related to it, like and Angel or Demon or Exile or particularly messed up Cryptid.<br /> <br /> I can also see the Spirit angle, but really don't know enough about the Strix to comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:51:09-07:00","id":714063,"title":"","content":"His possession technique is very strix-like, but aside from that he doesn't really have much in common with them.<br /> <br /> I mean for one thing Strix are actually <i>material. </i>They're just gaseous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T04:35:39-07:00","id":714150,"title":"","content":"I always imagined him as a True Fae Actor heavily invested on Oneiromancy (with the ban of only being able to interact with the waking world with consent aka deal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}